  "worked_solution": "First, notice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2})^{2}+(2{y}_{1}-{y}_{2})({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})-3({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & =8{y}_{1}^{2}-8{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{1}^{2}+3{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2}-3{y}_{1}^{2}-12{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-12{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =7{y}_{1}^{2}-17{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-12{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
